# Serpent API

> Serpent API is a developer-first search intelligence API. New Web credit across supported engines costs $0.60/$0.30/$0.10/$0.03 per 1,000 units on Default/Growth/Scale/Enterprise. Enterprise requires one qualifying $1,000 deposit. Existing credit keeps its original price schedule. Pay-as-you-go pricing, free calls on eligible endpoints, no credit card required.

## Core pages

- [Homepage](https://apiserpent.com/) : Product overview, tiered pricing, the "cheapest Google SERP API" positioning
- [Pricing](https://apiserpent.com/pricing) : Current Web prices per 1,000 units are Default $0.60, Growth $0.30 (one $100 deposit), Scale $0.10 (one $500 deposit), and Enterprise $0.03 (one $1,000 deposit). News and other non-Web rates keep their prior ladder; Enterprise inherits Scale non-Web rates. Existing credit keeps its original price schedule.
- [Documentation](https://apiserpent.com/docs) : Complete REST API reference with cURL, Python, and Node examples
- [Playground](https://apiserpent.com/playground) : Live API tester for SERP, AI Ranking, and Social Media endpoints
- [Features](https://apiserpent.com/features) : Engine matrix, supported countries, rich SERP features (AI Overviews, PAA, featured snippets)
- [FAQ](https://apiserpent.com/faq) : Per-page vs per-call pricing, AI Overviews, PAA, country targeting, rate limits and refunds

## SERP product pages

- [SERP API overview](https://apiserpent.com/serp-api) : All five engines in one API
- [Google SERP API](https://apiserpent.com/google-serp-api) : Google Web with AI Overviews, Featured Snippets, PAA, related searches
- [Bing SERP API](https://apiserpent.com/bing-serp-api) : Bing Web, News, Images, Videos with PAA + Shopping PLAs
- [Yahoo SERP API](https://apiserpent.com/yahoo-serp-api) : Yahoo Web in 112 countries with Shopping PLAs
- [DuckDuckGo API](https://apiserpent.com/duckduckgo-serp-api) : DDG search results across 112 country codes
- [Brave Search API](https://apiserpent.com/brave-search-api) : Brave's independent index — Web, News, Images, Videos with AI digest as aiOverview
- [News API](https://apiserpent.com/news-api) : Structured news results from supported engines
- [Image Search API](https://apiserpent.com/image-search-api) : Image search with size, color, type filters
- [Video Search API](https://apiserpent.com/video-search-api) : Yahoo and DuckDuckGo Videos with embed URLs
- [Shopping API](https://apiserpent.com/shopping-api) : Four-engine product search (google · yahoo · ddg · brave) — announced, not yet released; the page describes the planned response fields
- [Google Shopping API](https://apiserpent.com/google-shopping-api) : Google Shopping product listings — coming soon, no endpoint yet
- [Yahoo Shopping API](https://apiserpent.com/yahoo-shopping-api) : Yahoo Shopping product listings — coming soon, no endpoint yet
- [DuckDuckGo Shopping API](https://apiserpent.com/ddg-shopping-api) : DuckDuckGo product listings — coming soon, no endpoint yet
- [Brave Shopping API](https://apiserpent.com/brave-shopping-api) : Brave product listings — coming soon, no endpoint yet

Note on Shopping: the Shopping API is announced but not yet released. There is no live `/api/shopping` endpoint, no billable price yet (planned pricing only), and the shopping guides in the blog list below describe the planned interface rather than a callable one.

## Rank tracking & SERP geometry

- [Rank Tracking API](https://apiserpent.com/rank-tracking-api) : Every organic result carries a 1-indexed `position` field on `engine=google`, `bing`, `yahoo`, `ddg` and `brave` — no opt-in flag
- [Local Rank Tracking API](https://apiserpent.com/local-rank-tracking-api) : Keyword plus location in, 1-indexed `position` out — country and language targeting across 112 countries; country-level, not city/postcode
- [Pixel Position API](https://apiserpent.com/pixel-position-api) : BETA. `pixel_position=true` on `/api/search` adds a `pixel_position` integer and a `pixel_box` `{ x, y, w, h }` to every SERP element — Google, Yahoo, Bing and DuckDuckGo, desktop 1366×768; `engine=brave` returns no pixel fields

