## Social media APIs

- [Social Media API overview](https://apiserpent.com/social-media-api) : One REST API for YouTube and Instagram data — search, video, channel and profile endpoints
- [YouTube API](https://apiserpent.com/youtube-api) : Search videos, channels, playlists without Google quota
- [Instagram API](https://apiserpent.com/instagram-api) : Profile scraper — bio, followers, engagement, recent posts
- [LinkedIn API](https://apiserpent.com/linkedin-api) : Company firmographics, job postings, and public profile data via one REST endpoint
- [TikTok API](https://apiserpent.com/tiktok-api) : TikTok profile, video, hashtag, search and music data as JSON — the five endpoints and their billable rates. Basic `/profile` and `/video` calls usually return in seconds; optional field groups and list requests can take longer and support a job form when available
- [X (Twitter) API](https://apiserpent.com/x-api) : Single post by id or URL and public profile by handle, as JSON — lookup only: no post search, no full timelines, no followers list. Billed per request, never per item: $0.10/1K for a post ($0.09 Growth, $0.07 Scale), $0.10/1K for a profile flat at every tier, $0.15/1K with `hydrate=true`, also flat. Both endpoints also run as background jobs through `POST /api/bulk/jobs` under the keys `x_tweet` and `x_profile`; there is no `/api/x/*/async` twin, and since X has no depth parameter a job buys a bigger time budget and one submission for many items rather than more data per call
- [Reddit API](https://apiserpent.com/reddit-api) : Subreddit listings, post comments, post search, user and community summaries as JSON, billed per call rather than per item returned. One rate for all five endpoints — $0.12/1K on Default, $0.108 Growth, $0.084 Scale. `search`, `user` and `subreddit` are that flat charge at any depth; `posts` and `comments` are charged one unit per started block of 25 items, so `limit=100` is four blocks ($0.48/1K). Every operation has an `/async` twin at the same block price, with `limit` up to 250 on posts and 1000 on comments

## Marketplace data

- [Amazon Scraper API](https://apiserpent.com/amazon-scraper-api) : Amazon product, search and bestseller data as JSON across 22 marketplaces, billed per request rather than per result — `/api/amazon/search`, `/api/amazon/product` and `/api/amazon/bestsellers` are live, and the rates shown on the page are the billable rates

## Local business data

- [Google Maps API](https://apiserpent.com/google-maps-api) : Ranked place search (up to 100), one rich place record, and paged reviews as normalized JSON

